From d159b46dc6658edb3178548413fbd22d73c85e5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:06:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] G2c-blockers: share one blocker walk per sweep pass
 + per-task decoded-run cache
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

sweep_shared_blockers derived blocker_states three times per pass (once per lane), each walking ~1.4k runs of
every task that asserted in the 14-day lookback with ~225 SQL statements. On the hub's busy default board the
revision gates miss nearly every tick, so this cost was paid on every dirty tick (design t_01a1d563324d7e8e
§1 option 1, §2 P2, R13; card t_01a1db0791738a4f under G2b t_01a1d701bfd0abb6).

- hermes_cli/kanban_blocker_rows.py (new): per-board-file cache of each asserting task's decoded own rows (run
  tuples with effect/bid/epochs/explicit-clear flag, the assertion-scan rows with provider/model/lane/reason/uid,
  and the task status). Refreshed with kanban_task_change.changed_since in one BEGIN..COMMIT snapshot; FULL on
  an untrusted cursor (R7), an alias-snapshot change, or a caller window earlier than the fill cutoff. Never
  stored from inside a caller transaction or with a None cursor; swapped immutably under a lock with a
  never-backwards compare. Memory bounded to tasks with an in-window assertion. The window, walk, routes,
  condition_met evidence (live: heartbeats move its MAX(id) without marking), check clears and the fence
  rerun every call.
- blocker_states: the walk (_walk) runs on those rows and is shared by the lanes of one pass via
  kanban_blocker_inputs.read, keyed with the commit counters, file identity, alias snapshot and the set of
  in-window assertion run ids; each consumer gets a deep copy and applies check clears and the fence itself.
  The kanban_blocker_inputs docstring rule now reads: derived BlockerState is retained only within one pass
  under that key, never across passes (G2b owner sign-off on the card).
- _read_assertion_tokens and the quota fence read the decoded rows (same cohort and identity formulas) instead of
  re-querying and re-decoding every assertion row; the fence's per-row run_identity query becomes the row's uid.
- The three lanes ask foreign_among(conn, behind ids) (primary-key reads of only the parked cards) instead of
  kanban_wake_check.foreign_ids, a full tasks scan whose memo misses on every dirty tick.
- scripts/kanban_reclaim_replay_bench.py: --blockers N dirty-tick sweep_shared_blockers case.

Bench (hub, copy of the default board, t01a1d701_dirty.py, N=11, same script and copy):
  sweep_shared_blockers dirty median 38.68-40.74 ms before (deployed 854519ff) -> 4.96-5.41 ms after.
  kanban_reclaim_replay_bench.py --blockers 15: 40.77 ms -> 4.51 ms median.
  t01a1d701_blk.py lanes: states 13.5 -> 1.8, checks 12.3 -> 2.7, release 11.7 -> 1.9, probe 13.7 -> 2.4,
  sweep 31.9 -> 4.4 ms.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_blocker_rows.py compares cached against cold derivations (cross-task write,
window exit with no write, earlier caller now, alias change, equal ended_at tie by run id, late heartbeat after
condition_met, txn write+rollback+rev reuse, FULL_MARK/file replace/shm/task delete, two-thread race, CAS,
randomized write sequences, walk sharing and lane-write invalidation, window-keyed walk, held-set bound);
12 targeted mutants of the cache and walk are each killed.
